    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** serving as our primary engines. **Yordan Alvarez** (71.83) is the clear anchor, leveraging an elite 0.421 xwOBA against a vulnerable matchup with Leiter. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.52) offers a high-upside profile despite hitting lower in the order; the combination of a favorable dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and a slow delivery from Burke, S, creates an elite environment for his stolen base prowess\u2014a critical priority given the league's scarcity of speed. **Junior Caminero** (65.41) rounds out our top-tier tier, benefiting from a move up to the #2 hole and a favorable matchup against Junk, which helps mitigate park factor concerns.\n\nOur bench optimization was highlighted by a tight decision regarding **Chase Meidroth** (41.84). While his projected efficiency crossed our marginal threshold, he ultimately yielded to the superior platoon and order-based projections of **Colt Keith** (58.17) and **Luke Raley** (60.21). Both players are positioned to exploit favorable SP xERAs, whereas **Chase Meidroth** faces a tougher matchup against the well-regarded Cabrera, E. We remain cautious regarding **Trea Turner** (54.84) and **Kyle Schwarber** (53.13); both face the significant hurdle of Ashcraft, B, whose skill level imposes an 11% penalty on their base projections. Furthermore, we continue to monitor the status of **Lars Nootbaar**, who remains shelved on the IL, while **Christian Yelich** and **Gary Sanchez** are excluded from today\u2019s lineup due to rest and platoon considerations. Managers should watch for late-breaking weather patterns, though our current projections remain locked for this 5x5 Roto push.",
